le":"The people bring offerings","setting":["camp"],"on_stage_named":["moses"],"on_stage_unnamed":["israelites"],"mentioned_only":[]},{"start":"35:30","end":"35:35","title":"Bezalel's skill announced","setting":["camp"],"on_stage_named":["moses","bezalel","oholiab"],"on_stage_unnamed":["israelites"],"mentioned_only":["yahweh"]},{"start":"36:1","end":"36:7","title":"Craftsmen receive offerings","setting":["camp"],"on_stage_named":["moses","bezalel","oholiab"],"on_stage_unnamed":["israelites"],"mentioned_only":[]},{"start":"36:8","end":"36:38","title":"Construction of the tabernacle","setting":["tabernacle"],"on_stage_named":[],"on_stage_unnamed":["israelites"],"mentioned_only":[]},{"start":"37:1","end":"37:29","title":"Bezalel makes the ark and furniture","setting":["tabernacle"],"on_stage_named":["bezalel"],"on_stage_unnamed":[],"mentioned_only":[]},{"start":"38:1","end":"38:20","title":"The altar and court","setting":["tabernacle"],"on_stage_named":[],"on_stage_unnamed":[],"mentioned_only":[]},{"start":"38:21","end":"38:31","title":"Accounting of materials","setting":["tabernacle"],"on_stage_named":["bezalel","oholiab"],"on_stage_unnamed":[],"mentioned_only":["ithamar"]},{"start":"39:1","end":"39:31","title":"Priestly garments made","setting":["tabernacle"],"on_stage_named":["aaron"],"on_stage_unnamed":[],"mentioned_only":[]},{"start":"39:32","end":"39:43","title":"Work completed and blessed","setting":["tabernacle"],"on_stage_named":["moses"],"on_stage_unnamed":["israelites"],"mentioned_only":[]},{"start":"40:1","end":"40:16","title":"Yahweh commands the setting up","setting":["tabernacle"],"on_stage_named":["yahweh","moses","aaron"],"on_stage_unnamed":[],"mentioned_only":[]},{"start":"40:17","end":"40:33","title":"The tabernacle is raised","setting":["tabernacle"],"on_stage_named":["moses","aaron"],"on_stage_unnamed":[],"mentioned_only":[]},{"start":"40:34","end":"40:38","title":"Glory fills the tabernacle; cloud guides","setting":["tabernacle","wilderness"],"on_stage_named":["yahweh","moses"],"on_stage_unnamed":["israelites"],"mentioned_only":[]}],"brief":{"era":"Late Bronze Age, roughly 13th century BCE, the Exodus narrative and wilderness wanderings.","place":"Egypt (Goshen, Rameses, Pithom), the Red Sea, the Sinai wilderness, Midian, and Mount Sinai.","dress":"Egyptian court: linen kilts, collars, headdresses for Pharaoh and officials. Hebrews: simple wool or linen tunics and cloaks. Priests: fine linen tunics, sashes, turbans, the blue-purple-scarlet ephod and breastplate with twelve stones.","buildings_and_objects":"Brick storage cities; the tabernacle with acacia-wood boards, gold-overlaid ark with cherubim on the mercy seat, golden lampstand with almond-blossom branches, bronze altar, linen court; tents, baskets of papyrus and tar, shepherds' wells.","depiction_rules":["Yahweh must never be drawn as a human figure; show divine presence only as fire, cloud, pillar, smoke, glory or light.","Angels may be shown as human-like messengers or as the fire and cloud themselves; avoid faces of God.","Moses' face may shine with light after Sinai; render as radiance without a visible deity.","Plagues should be vivid and literal (blood-red river, frogs, lice, flies, boils, hail with fire, locusts, darkness).","Ark, cherubim and tabernacle must follow the described pattern, not an invented design.","Israelites and Egyptians should be distinguishable by dress; Egyptians wear court attire and are often in chariots.","The golden calf is an idol; depict it as an image of a bull-calf, never as Yahweh."]}}}